SCHEDULE: {"1":"Gus","2":"Elif","3":"Cara","4":"Ann","5":"Ben","6":"Finn","7":"Dev"}
CONFIDENCE: 97

The derivation is short. Ben must be in slot 3–6 because Cara and Elif are both before him. Finn is right after Ben, and Dev is after Finn, so Dev is in slot 6 or 7. Ben at 3 and 4 both fail, and Ben at 6 leaves no room for Dev, so Ben is in slot 5. That forces Finn to 6 and Dev to 7. Gus and Elif must both come before Ben and be at least 3 slots from him, which leaves Gus at 1 and Elif at 2. Cara is then at 3, and Ann at 4, which is 3 slots from Dev. Every constraint checks out against this schedule.
